@* REQ-UI-038 (BRD-90): applies the stored theme and accent to <html>. It renders nothing and sits
   OUTSIDE the Router on purpose — the app has two layouts (MainLayout for the shell, AuthLayout for
   /login, /register and the first-run wizard), and mounting this in either one would leave the other
   rendering light on a dark install. Here it runs once per window, for every route. *@
<ThemeInitializer />

@* REQ-FN-035: was typeof(Program).Assembly — Program was the Blazor Server web host and is gone.
   Anchoring on this component keeps the router pointed at the head assembly regardless of host. *@
<Router AppAssembly="typeof(Routes).Assembly">
    <Found Context="routeData">
        @* REQ-FN-036 / BRD-129: there is no route protection here and none in the shell. The app
           opens straight into a usable workspace with no account: launch never resolves to /login,
           and no route is split into an authenticated and an anonymous variant. /login is an
           ordinary page like any other — reached only when the user picks "Sign in" from the
           Account area to activate a licence. What used to live here (a comment describing the
           IRouteGuard login bounce that MainLayout applied on every navigation) described a gate
           that no longer exists; IRouteGuard retains only the capability check that REQ-FN-041
           removes with the rest of the retired role stack. *@
        <RouteView RouteData="routeData" DefaultLayout="typeof(Layout.MainLayout)" />
        <FocusOnNavigate RouteData="routeData" Selector="h1" />
    </Found>
</Router>
